From a37a23c42fc0a18d1360eea7991a4b04891bf2b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 13:34:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add CA1881: prefer MemoryExtensions.Split over counted
 string.Split

Implements the analyzer approved in dotnet/runtime#85487
(API review 2023-06-01). Per the review, the initial version only
reports string.Split calls that pass a count, since the span-based
MemoryExtensions.Split/SplitAny overloads with a Span<Range> destination
are an exact analogue of those. Category Performance, severity Info,
no code fix.

The rule is C#-only, is skipped when the span overloads don't exist
(pre-.NET 8), and is not reported inside expression trees, async
methods/lambdas/local functions, or iterators, where span locals
can't be used.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
